The organisation knows its business context and the requirements of its interested parties, and it has defined what its information security management system (ISMS) covers.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs an ISMS, for example to meet NIS2 or to get an ISO/IEC 27001 certificate. A team that only needs the central controls for its products does not need it.

== How to implement

Write the business context analysis. It describes the business of the organisation, the internal and external issues, and the interested parties and their requirements. Its last section defines the scope of the ISMS: the organisational units, the locations, the services, and the information systems, with a reason for each exclusion.

{{#report}}
  "name": "ismsa/reports/createEvidence",
  "identifier": "ismsa_document_business-context-analysis",
  "template": "ismsa/templates/businessContextAnalysis",
  "buttonLabel": "Create the business context analysis"
{{/report}}

Check that the business context analysis is approved, and that it is reviewed when the business or the requirements change.

